<title>USA: NORTHERN TRUST SAYS NAMED CUSTODIAN BY U.K. FUND.</title>
<headline>NORTHERN TRUST SAYS NAMED CUSTODIAN BY U.K. FUND.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Trust Corp said the 1.1 billion (sterling) Cable and Wireless Superannuation Fund, located in the United Kingdom, has named the Chicago-based bank as its global custodian.</p>
<p>Northern Trust said it was selected from a short list of three banks chosen after quantitative analysis of tenders submitted by nine banks.</p>
<p>Northern Trust provides custody services for more than 600 institutional investors worldwide. It has more than $898 billion in assets under custody.</p>
<p>(Sterling=$1.6015 U.S.) -- ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
